# 3. THERAPIST-USER CONNECTION SYSTEM

Implement TWO invitation workflows.

## Workflow A: Therapist invites a user

1. Verified therapist opens their dashboard.
2. Selects "Invite a Client".
3. Enters the intended recipient's contact information.
4. Selects the purpose of the invitation.
5. Generates a secure, time-limited invitation.
6. User receives an invitation.
7. User logs into or registers for ClearPath.
8. User reviews the therapist's verified identity.
9. User reviews requested access permissions.
10. User accepts or rejects the connection.

## Workflow B: User invites a therapist

1. User enters Recover & Rebuild.
2. Opens "My Professional Support".
3. Selects "Connect My Therapist".
4. Searches the verified professional directory or invites an existing therapist.
5. Therapist receives the invitation.
6. Therapist authenticates their professional account.
7. Therapist accepts.
8. User authorizes the required information-sharing permissions.
9. The care relationship becomes active.

The therapist must not receive access simply because an invitation was sent.

Both parties must complete the required acceptance steps.

Implement invitation expiration, cancellation and secure verification.

Never expose whether an unrelated person has a ClearPath account through a public search.

